   305→            acceptance_criteria:
   306→              - id: ac-command-field
   307→                given: Command object in batch array
   308→                when: The command field is parsed
   309→                then: Field matches a known mutating CLI command path such as item add or task note
   310→              - id: ac-args-mapping
   311→                given: Command object with args
   312→                when: Args are mapped to CLI parameters
   313→                then: Keys map to flag names without -- prefix, positional args use their documented argument name
   314→              - id: ac-unknown-command
   315→                given: Command object with unrecognized command path
   316→                when: Validation runs
   317→                then: Error identifies the unknown command and suggests similar valid commands
   318→              - id: ac-missing-required
   319→                given: Command object missing a required arg
   320→                when: Validation runs
   321→                then: Error identifies which arg is missing for which command
   322→              - id: ac-id-field
   323→                given: Command object with optional id field
   324→                when: Batch output is rendered
   325→                then: The id appears in per-command results for correlation
   326→            status:
   327→              maturity: draft
   328→              implementation: implemented
   329→          - _ulid: 01KGR05MG2NNH5AVVC159HYQEN
   330→            slugs:
   331→              - batch-allowed-commands
   332→            title: Batch Allowed Commands
   333→            type: requirement
   334→            tags: []
   335→            description: >
   336→              Defines which CLI commands are allowed in batch mode. Commands are classified as
   337→              mutating or read-only based on whether they modify kspec state (YAML files in the
   338→              shadow branch). All mutating commands are allowed. Read-only commands and meta/system
   339→              commands are rejected during validation. The classification is determined by command
   340→              metadata, not a hardcoded list.
   341→            depends_on: []
   342→            implements: []
   343→            relates_to: []
   344→            tests: []
   345→            traits: []
   346→            notes: []
   347→            created: 2026-02-05T22:53:37.154Z
   348→            acceptance_criteria:
   349→              - id: ac-allowlist
   350→                given: A mutating command (item add, task start, derive, inbox promote, etc.)
   351→                when: Used in batch
   352→                then: Command is accepted and executed
   353→              - id: ac-denylist
   354→                given: A non-mutating command (item get, task list, search, validate, etc.)
   355→                when: Used in batch
   356→                then: Validation rejects with message explaining batch is for mutating operations only
   357→              - id: ac-batch-itself
   358→                given: A batch command nested inside a batch
   359→                when: Used in batch
   360→                then: Validation rejects with message that batch cannot be nested
   361→            status:
   362→              maturity: draft
   363→              implementation: implemented
   364→        acceptance_criteria:
   365→          - id: ac-stdin
   366→            given: JSON array piped via stdin
   367→            when: kspec batch runs with no --file or --commands flag
   368→            then: Commands are read from stdin and executed in order
   369→          - id: ac-file
   370→            given: --file flag with path to JSON file
   371→            when: kspec batch --file commands.json runs
   372→            then: Commands are read from the file and executed in order
   373→          - id: ac-inline
   374→            given: --commands flag with JSON string
   375→            when: kspec batch --commands with inline JSON runs
   376→            then: Inline JSON is parsed and commands execute
   377→          - id: ac-stop-on-error
   378→            given: Default mode (no --continue flag) with 5 commands where command 3 fails at runtime
   379→            when: Batch executes
   380→            then: "In atomic mode: all changes rolled back. In immediate mode: commands 1-2 committed, commands
   381→              4-5 not executed. Exit code is 1"
   382→          - id: ac-continue
   383→            given: Immediate mode (--continue implies --no-atomic) with 5 commands where command 3 fails at
   384→              runtime
   385→            when: Batch executes
   386→            then: All 5 commands are attempted, command 3 failure is recorded, other commands succeed, exit code
   387→              is 1
   388→          - id: ac-prevalidate
   389→            given: Batch with 3 commands where command 2 has invalid syntax
   390→            when: kspec batch runs
   391→            then: Validation fails before any execution, no commands run, error identifies the invalid command
   392→              by index, exit code is 1
   393→          - id: ac-dry-run
   394→            given: --dry-run flag with valid batch
   395→            when: kspec batch --dry-run runs
   396→            then: All commands are validated but not executed, output shows what would run, no state changes
   397→              occur
   398→          - id: ac-forward-ref
   399→            given: Batch where command 2 references slug created by command 1
   400→            when: kspec batch runs
   401→            then: Pre-validation recognizes the forward reference as valid, execution succeeds for both commands
   402→          - id: ac-single-commit
   403→            given: Atomic mode (default) with 3 successful mutating commands
   404→            when: Batch completes successfully
   405→            then: A single shadow branch commit is created containing all changes (not 3 separate commits)
   406→          - id: ac-partial-commit
   407→            given: Immediate mode with --continue, commands 1-2 succeed, command 3 fails
   408→            when: Batch completes with partial success
   409→            then: 2 individual commits (commands 1-2), no commit for command 3
   410→          - id: ac-mutating-only
   411→            given: Batch containing a read-only command like item get
   412→            when: kspec batch runs
   413→            then: Validation rejects with error identifying the non-mutating command
   414→          - id: ac-confirmation-suppressed
   415→            given: Batch containing a command that normally requires confirmation (e.g., item delete without
   416→              --force)
   417→            when: kspec batch runs
   418→            then: Command executes without prompting for confirmation (batch mode is implicitly non-interactive)
   419→          - id: ac-invalid-json
   420→            given: Malformed JSON input (from any source)
   421→            when: kspec batch runs
   422→            then: Parse error with line/position info if available, exit code 1, no commands executed
   423→          - id: ac-empty-batch
   424→            given: Empty JSON array []
   425→            when: kspec batch runs
   426→            then: Error message says batch contains no commands, exit code 1
   427→          - id: ac-default-atomic
   428→            given: kspec batch runs without --no-atomic
   429→            when: Batch executes
   430→            then: "Atomic mode: commands execute against isolated copy of state"
   431→          - id: ac-atomic-rollback
   432→            given: Atomic mode, 5 cmds where cmd 3 fails
   433→            when: Batch encounters failure
   434→            then: ALL changes discarded, no shadow commit, state identical to before batch, exit 1
   435→          - id: ac-atomic-isolation
   436→            given: Atomic mode, commands modifying state
   437→            when: Batch is executing
   438→            then: Modifications in isolated copy; other kspec operations see original state
   439→          - id: ac-no-atomic-flag
   440→            given: --no-atomic flag provided
   441→            when: kspec batch runs
   442→            then: "Immediate mode: per-command commits, no rollback"
   443→          - id: ac-immediate-per-commit
   444→            given: Immediate mode, 3 successful commands
   445→            when: Batch completes
   446→            then: 3 individual shadow commits (one per command)
   447→          - id: ac-immediate-no-rollback
   448→            given: Immediate mode, 5 cmds where cmd 3 fails
   449→            when: Batch stops
   450→            then: Commands 1-2 remain committed, cmds 4-5 not executed, exit 1
   451→          - id: ac-continue-implies-immediate
   452→            given: --continue without --no-atomic
   453→            when: kspec batch runs
   454→            then: Immediate mode activated implicitly with notice in output
   455→          - id: ac-json-mode-field
   456→            given: --json flag provided
   457→            when: Batch completes
   458→            then: "JSON output includes mode field: atomic or immediate"
